            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_004.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00014",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00014-alt",
              "text": "An aldehyde, R C H O reacts with chromium trioxide and hydronium ion to form a carboxylic acid, R C O O H."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_005.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00015",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00015-alt",
              "text": "An R, R prime carbonyl reacts with sodium borohydride, ethanol, then hydronium ion to form an alcohol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_006.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00016",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00016-alt",
              "text": "An R, R prime carbonyl reacts with R double prime Mg Br and ether, then hydronium ion to form an alcohol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_007.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00017",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00017-alt",
              "text": "An R, R prime carbonyl reacts with H C N to form a compound with C bonded to R, R prime, O H, and C N."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_008.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00018",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00018-alt",
              "text": "An R, R prime carbonyl reacts with N H 2 R double prime to form imine: C bonded to R, R prime, and double bonded to N R double prime."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_009.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00019",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00019-alt",
              "text": "A carbonyl with one R group and one substituent with an alpha hydrogen reacts with H N R prime 2 to give an enamine."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_010.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00020",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00020-alt",
              "text": "An R, R prime carbonyl reacts with H 2 N N H 2 to form alkane with R and R prime groups and two hydrogens on former carbonyl carbon."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_011.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00021",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00021-alt",
              "text": "An R, R prime carbonyl reacts with 2 equivalents of R double prime alcohol in acid to give acetal with substituents R, R prime, and two O R double prime."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_012.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00022",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00022-alt",
              "text": "A carbonyl compound reacts with phosphorus ylide in the presence of tetrahydro furan to form an alkene and a phosphoryl group linked to three phenyl groups."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_013.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00023",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00023-alt",
              "text": "An alpha beta-unsaturated compound reacts with an amine to form a compound with carbonyl and beta amine group."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_014.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00024",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00024-alt",
              "text": "An alpha beta-unsaturated compound reacts with water to form a compound with carbonyl and beta hydroxyl group."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_015.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00025",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00225:alt:fig-00025-alt",
              "text": "An alpha beta-unsaturated compound reacts with R dash 2 C u L i, ether and hydronium ion to form a compound with carbonyl and beta R prime group."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_EC_016.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
